      "side": 1,
      "message": "We shouldn\u0027t add hermeticity issues to the build, and depending on outside tooling is even worse than what\u0027s happening here. I\u0027m also not sure how brittle it is to run `rustfmt` on code and then expect it to match a pre-recorded version of the code, because `rustfmt` can also change in subtle ways between releases (particularly if you\u0027re depending on any unspecified defaults).\n\nCould we disable the text comparison tests for now (or at least the text-comparing portions of them) on Android? If not, we really need someone to work on getting a proper rule added for `rustfmt` added to Soong where you can then fix the pdl build here to call the non-sandboxed (i.e. non-genrule-invoked) `rustfmt`.",
